message: >-
  If you use the software, public controls, or study design, cite this release and the exact
  Kaggle dataset or notebook version used in your analysis.
title: "Humor Genome Wave 2: reproducible humor-structure research and integration toolkit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amarel
    given-names: "Taylor S."
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/aidonerightcorp/humorvibes-jestry"
url: "https://github.com/aidonerightcorp/humorvibes-jestry/releases/tag/v0.8.0"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - humor research
  - Gemma
  - reproducible research
  - multilingual NLP
  - human evaluation
  - FastAPI
abstract: >-
  A public research release and deployable toolkit for studying humor structure without treating
  model surprisal as funniness. It includes rights-filtered data, executable Kaggle notebooks,
  deterministic CC0 controls, adversarial and multimodal contracts, human-study launch tooling,
  provider-neutral integrations, an API, and container-orchestration manifests.
